  <!-- 0.50.5 to 0.50.6 (.github#2512): NOT the usual republish bump. 0.50.5 IS A PERMANENT
       TWO-OF-THREE SET and must not be adopted. The bump above moved this scalar and did NOT update
       FS.GG.Coord.Cli.fsproj's PackageReleaseNotes, which still opened "0.50.4" — so at release time
       check-engine-release-notes (.github#1762) correctly refused to publish the engine, AFTER
       FS.GG.Kit 0.50.5 and FS.GG.Drivers 0.50.5 had already published to the feeds. Tags are
       immutable and .github#1772's sibling-tag precondition requires all three tags at the SAME
       commit, so 0.50.5 cannot be completed from a corrected tree: correcting the notes needs a new
       commit, and that is a new version. This is exactly the 0.50.1 shape, recorded verbatim in
       registry/dependencies.yml. 0.50.6 is that corrected cut — notes and scalar moved TOGETHER,
       which is the whole point — and it is the version the fleet should adopt.

       WHY IT COULD HAPPEN AT ALL, AND WHAT NOW PREVENTS IT. A PR-time arm of that same checker
       already existed (.github/workflows/engine-release-notes.yml), but its `paths:` filter did not
       select THIS FILE — only the project file. A bump that lands solely here therefore ran none of
       it, and the gate first spoke at release time, which is after the irrevocable part. Both that
       filter and the checker's own PATHS_SUBJECT now name this file, and check-paths-coherence rule
       (c) plus tests/engine-release-notes/run.sh keep the two from drifting apart again. -->
  <!-- 0.50.6 to 0.50.7 (.github#2526): same-line patch bump, the ordinary republish shape — same cause
       as 0.50.3 to 0.50.4 and 0.50.4 to 0.50.5 above, NOT the two-of-three repair immediately above.
       This PR edits pnext-item/SKILL.md, a kit-packed source, correcting three prose claims that call
